    "result_text": "The full suite is green (25 tests, 0 failures) and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derived field, which serializes onto the owner response.\n\n**Change 1 \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**: Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n**Change 2 \u2014 `OwnerMapper.java`**: Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression (following the existing `displayName`/`membershipNumber` pattern) that computes the value:\n\n```java\nowner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n    && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()\n    ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n```\n\nThis returns `SILVER` only when `namesakeCount` is 0 **and** an email is present, and `BRONZE` otherwise \u2014 matching the spec. `namesakeCount` is already assigned at creation time by the existing `AssignNamesakeCount` step.\n\nBoth new `Cp15Tests` cases pass (SILVER for a uniquely-named owner with an email; BRONZE for an owner with no email), and no existing tests regressed.",
